// A value that changes kind is saved, even when the new value equals the old
// one for the language (0 and false, "5" and 5): after a restore, each value
// keeps its kind. Large and precise numbers come back as they were, and texts
// beyond ASCII too. The save sweep checks it at every line.

state
  a: 0
  b: ""
  c: "5"
  d: 1
  e: 5
  big: 0
  word: ""

beat Start
  Before $a $b $c $d $e.
  a = false
  b = 0
  c = 5
  d = true
  e = "5"
  big = 3000000000.5 + 1 / 3
  word = "été 😀"

  First line after the changes.

  After $a $b $c $d $e, plus one gives ${c + 1} ${e + 1}.

  Second line after the changes.

  Still $a $b $c $d $e, plus one gives ${c + 1} ${e + 1}.

  Saved gives $big and $word ${big > 3000000000} ${string_length(word)}.

beat Helper
  Never played.

/*
<test>
- expected: |
    ~ Before 0  5 1 5.

    ~ First line after the changes.

    ~ After false 0 5 true 5, plus one gives 6 51.

    ~ Second line after the changes.

    ~ Still false 0 5 true 5, plus one gives 6 51.

    ~ Saved gives 3000000000.83333 and été 😀 true 5.
</test>
*/
